RAHasher (https://github.com/LeXofLeviafan/RAHasher)
  Copyright (c) LeXofLeviafan and the RALibretro / rcheevos contributors.
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.
  The full licence text ships alongside the binary as bin/RAHasher.COPYING,
  and bin/RAHasher.PROVENANCE.md pins the exact upstream release (1.8.3),
  with checksums and a link to its source.
  RAHasher is bundled unmodified at bin/RAHasher and is run as a SEPARATE
  EXECUTABLE over its command-line interface — CheevoDeck does not link
  against it and contains none of its code. Its GPL terms cover that binary
  alone; CheevoDeck's own source remains under the BSD-3 licence above.

chdman (https://github.com/mamedev/mame)
  Copyright (c) MAMEdev and the MAME contributors.
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 ONLY — MAME's
  COPYING states version 2 with no "or later" clause, so this is a different
  licence from RAHasher's above and ships as its own text.
  The full licence text ships alongside the binary as bin/chdman.COPYING, and
  bin/chdman.PROVENANCE.md pins the MAME release tag this binary was built
  from, with its checksum.
  chdman is built by me from that tag, stripped, bundled at bin/chdman and run
  as a SEPARATE EXECUTABLE over its command-line interface — CheevoDeck does
  not link against it and contains none of its code. Its GPL terms cover that
  binary alone; CheevoDeck's own source remains under the BSD-3 licence above.

Reference catalogues in dats/ (https://github.com/libretro/libretro-database)
  Copyright (c) the libretro-database contributors.
  Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International.
  The full licence text ships alongside the data as dats/LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt,
  and dats/PROVENANCE.md pins the upstream commit, records the per-file
  checksums, and states what was changed.
  THE DATA WAS MODIFIED: each DAT was parsed and re-emitted as gzipped JSON,
  with the md5 and sha1 columns and all remaining per-entry metadata dropped.
  Share-alike therefore applies to dats/, and anyone redistributing CheevoDeck
  inherits that obligation for those files. It does NOT reach CheevoDeck's own
  source, which is a separate work shipped alongside the database rather than
  an adaptation of it, and stays under the BSD-3 licence above.
  The underlying catalogues originate with the No-Intro, Redump and TOSEC
  projects; libretro-database mirrors them, and taking libretro's copy is what
  keeps everything here under one stated licence.

@decky/ui, @decky/api (https://github.com/SteamDeckHomebrew/decky-frontend-lib)
  Licensed under LGPL-2.1.
  https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html
  @decky/ui is loaded from the Decky runtime and is not distributed with
  this plugin. @decky/api is bundled into dist/index.js. This plugin's own
  source is published in full under the BSD-3 license above, and @decky/api's
  source is public, so the library can be replaced and the plugin rebuilt.
